   RESERVED FONT NAME — why one font here is renamed
            IBM Plex Mono carries the Reserved Font Name "IBM Plex". Subsetting a
            font counts as modifying it under OFL 1.1 clause 3, and a modified
            version may not use the reserved name. The subset shipped in this
            system is therefore renamed "Aninda Mono". The unmodified family name
            is kept as the next fallback in the stylesheet, so anyone who already
            has IBM Plex Mono installed gets the original.
            Literata and Noto Serif Bengali carry no reserved name and keep theirs.

